From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toxpox <toxpox@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 16 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] configs: am67a_t3_gem_o1_a53: enable the legacy image format

ARCH_K3 selects FIT_SIGNATURE on ARM64, which clears the default of
LEGACY_IMAGE_FORMAT. select_ramdisk() then recognises the uImage that
update-initramfs writes as a legacy image, refuses to parse it, and falls
through to handing the kernel the payload with its 64-byte header still
attached:

  Initramfs unpacking failed: invalid magic at start of compressed archive

The Kconfig entry describes exactly this case: "If a board needs the legacy
image format support in this case, enable it here." Enable it, so the stock
config/bootscripts/boot-k3.cmd uInitrd path works without an override.

FIT_SIGNATURE stays enabled, but legacy images are unsigned. The board now
also accepts the unsigned uInitrd format produced by Armbian.

Signed-off-by: Toxpox <toxpox@outlook.com>
---
 configs/am67a_t3_gem_o1_a53_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/configs/am67a_t3_gem_o1_a53_defconfig b/configs/am67a_t3_gem_o1_a53_defconfig
--- a/configs/am67a_t3_gem_o1_a53_defconfig
+++ b/configs/am67a_t3_gem_o1_a53_defconfig
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@ CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND="run distro_bootcmd"
 CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_LEN=0x2000000
 CONFIG_EXT4_WRITE=y
 CONFIG_LZO=y
+CONFIG_LEGACY_IMAGE_FORMAT=y
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_KEYED=y
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_PROMPT="Press SPACE to abort autoboot in %d seconds\n"
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_DELAY_STR="d"
-- 
Armbian
